From: postmarketOS rhodep port
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm6375-motorola-rhodep: add ramoops

Add a pstore/ramoops region so that the tail of the kernel log and any
panic survive a reboot. Without this a bootloop is undebuggable: the ABL
rewrites the cmdline to console=null, so nothing reaches a serial console
either, and there is no way to see why the kernel died.

After a failed boot, flash a kernel that does boot (which also needs this
node) and read /sys/fs/pstore/.

The region is the one the downstream Motorola kernel uses for this very
device: include/dt-bindings/moto/moto-mem-reserve.h defines

	RAMOOPS_CONSOLE_SIZE	0x40000
	RAMOOPS_PMSG_SIZE	0x40000
	RAMOOPS_RECORD_SIZE	0x3f800
	RAMOOPS_SIZE		(console + pmsg + record) = 0xbf800
	RAMOOPS_BASE_ADDR	0xaf000000

and blair-pm6125-moto-common-overlay.dtsi (blair = SM6375, rhodep's base
DT is blair-moto-rhodep-base.dts) instantiates the ramoops node there
with no-map. That is the address the bootloader is known to preserve
across a warm reset. The generic holi.dtsi/blair.dtsi node at
0xd0000000 is explicitly deleted on Motorola boards
(blair-moto-base.dts: /delete-node/ ramoops) and is NOT preserved, which
is why nothing was ever recovered from it.

Differences from the vendor node, on purpose:

 - pmsg is not used (CONFIG_PSTORE_PMSG is off), so its 0x40000 are given
   to the console buffer instead: a full mainline boot log with
   ignore_loglevel does not fit in 256 KiB.
 - max-reason = <5> (KMSG_DUMP_MAX) instead of no-dump-oops, so a dump
   record is written on oops, emergency and even on an orderly reboot.
   The last one makes the black box self-testable: reboot normally and a
   dmesg-ramoops-0 file must appear.
 - mem-type = <1> (unbuffered) so console bytes are written straight to
   DRAM. With the default write-combining mapping the last writes before
   a hard reset can still sit in a WC buffer and be lost, which is
   exactly the window we need to see.

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6375-motorola-rhodep.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6375-motorola-rhodep.dts
@@ -99,6 +99,34 @@
 			reg = <0 0x85200000 0 0xc00000>;
 			no-map;
 		};
+
+		/*
+		 * Black box for debugging boot loops: pstore/ramoops keeps the
+		 * tail of the console log and the panic in RAM, and both
+		 * survive a reboot. After a failed boot they can be read from a
+		 * kernel that does boot, under /sys/fs/pstore/.
+		 *
+		 * Address and sizes come from the downstream Motorola kernel
+		 * for this device (dt-bindings/moto/moto-mem-reserve.h:
+		 * RAMOOPS_BASE_ADDR 0xaf000000, RAMOOPS_SIZE 0xbf800), which is
+		 * the region the Motorola bootloader preserves. The 0xd0000000
+		 * node from holi.dtsi/blair.dtsi is deleted on Motorola boards
+		 * and is not preserved.
+		 *
+		 * The whole 0xbf800 is split between console (0x80000) and one
+		 * dump record (0x3f800); pmsg is unused.
+		 */
+		ramoops@af000000 {
+			compatible = "ramoops";
+			reg = <0x0 0xaf000000 0x0 0xbf800>;
+			no-map;
+			console-size = <0x80000>;
+			record-size = <0x3f800>;
+			pmsg-size = <0x0>;
+			ftrace-size = <0x0>;
+			mem-type = <1>;
+			max-reason = <5>;
+		};
 	};
 
 	panel_vci: panel-vci-regulator {
